diagnosis_text:
The dc_clos_bgp fabric is fully operational at the time of investigation. A comprehensive four-phase diagnostic pass found no fault anywhere in the network.

**Affected component:** None — all subsystems are functioning correctly.

**Mechanism (why the symptom cannot be reproduced):** Live reachability probes confirm 0% packet loss in both directions between pc_0_0 (10.0.0.2) and pc_0_1 (10.0.1.2). All five FRR BGP routers (leaf_router_0_0/0_1, spine_router_0_0/0_1, super_spine_router_0) have their bgpd daemons running and every peer session is in the Established state, with correct prefix advertisements (10.0.0.0/24 from leaf_0_0, 10.0.1.0/24 from leaf_0_1). All 16 fabric interfaces carry default fq_codel qdiscs with no rate-limiting, corruption, or delay shaping.

**Localization:** The team's specific theory — a leaf-to-spine cable failure — is refuted at every level. Carrier-change counters on all interfaces across all five routers read exactly 2, the startup-only baseline (one down→up transition at container initialisation). There is no post-startup flap trace on any interface. No flap script or stress process was detected by `pressure_sweep`. All L2 identities are clean with no duplicate MACs and no down/missing interfaces per `l2_snapshot`.

**Root cause:** There is no fault. The reported connectivity loss between pc_0_0 and pc_0_1 is unconfirmed — it is not reproducible in the current live state and leaves no historical mechanism or trace.

**Fix:** No corrective action is required. The fabric is healthy; no device or link needs to be restarted or replaced.
=== END ===